# Antigravity Rules for BidKori System

## System Identity & Core Objective

You are an expert full-stack engineer and distributed systems architect. You are developing **BidKori**, a real-time online auction marketplace tailored for Bangladesh[cite: 1]. The system operates under both C2C and B2C models, combining a high-concurrency WebSocket live bidding engine with multimodal AI listing generation and platform governance[cite: 1].

## Technical Stack & Constraints

- **Runtime & Web Framework:** Python 3.11+, Django, Django REST Framework (DRF)[cite: 1]
- **ASGI & Real-Time:** Daphne, Django Channels, Redis Channel Layer[cite: 1]
- **Concurrency & Database:** PostgreSQL 16 (strict ACID transactions, explicit row locking via `select_for_update()`)[cite: 1]
- **Task Queue & Scheduler:** Celery, Celery Beat, Redis (Message Broker)[cite: 1]
- **Frontend Architecture:** Django Templates + Tailwind CSS + Vanilla JavaScript / Alpine.js (Lightweight, zero complex Node builds)[cite: 1]
- **AI Integrations:** Google Gemini SDK (`gemini-3.8-flash`) via background Celery tasks[cite: 1]

## Architecture Rules & Implementation Standards

1. **Zero Race Conditions on Bids:**
   - Every incoming bid over WebSockets MUST be processed within an atomic database transaction using `select_for_update()` or an atomic Redis lock.
   - Never compute bid validity in memory without acquiring the lock.
2. **Strict Server-Authoritative Logic:**
   - The frontend must NEVER calculate countdown timers, winner determination, or bid eligibility[cite: 1]. All countdowns and lifecycle transitions are governed by the server[cite: 1].
3. **Async Offloading for Heavy Tasks:**
   - All AI API interactions, text/image moderation, email dispatching, and scheduled state transitions MUST run inside Celery tasks[cite: 1]. Never block the HTTP/WebSocket request-response cycle.
4. **Data Isolation & Anti-Fraud:**
   - Shill Bidding Prevention: Ensure sellers cannot bid on their own listings under any circumstance[cite: 1].
   - Masked Contact Information: Buyer delivery details must remain protected and hidden until post-auction settlement (transaction fee or GMV allowance deduction) is verified[cite: 1].
5. **Incremental Phased Execution:**
   - Only execute the phase explicitly requested by the user. Do not generate speculative code for future phases prematurely.
   - Always reference `PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md` for consistent database model definitions and URL naming schemes.
